 class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951. On the middle of the county&rsquo;s grids, August to September, October to November and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those years. In 2025, January to February on the middle ran just 24% of normal, while June to July ran 159%. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, and grid 25341 bottomed out at 51% that year.</p>"}
